+/**
+ * Decides which distribution a project should serve for one installed entry.
+ *
+ * The rule, and the reasoning for each half:
+ *
+ * - The installed distribution is what a project serves when its open tasks are
+ *   pinned to it, or when it has no open tasks at all. That is the ordinary case
+ *   and it is unchanged.
+ * - When the installed bytes are NOT what the open tasks were admitted under,
+ *   and the project holds the version they were, the project serves the held
+ *   version. This is what "Project A stays on v1 while Project B starts on v2"
