+ *   shared, so a project that must not move cannot rely on it.
+ * - When SEVERAL held versions could be served, none is. Open tasks pinned to
+ *   different versions cannot all be satisfied by one registry, and choosing
+ *   between them would silently favour some tasks over others; the installed
+ *   version is served and the conflict is reported, so the affected tasks park
+ *   rather than run on a version nobody chose.
